permissions-delegated = Added through { $by }'s access management; it ends if that is taken away.
permission-help-clan-edit-profile = Change the clan's name and description.
permission-help-clan-read-members = See the clan's member directory.
permission-help-clan-invite = Invite people to join.
permission-help-clan-revoke-invitation = Cancel pending invitations before they are accepted.
permission-help-clan-remove-member = Remove ordinary members and end their clan access. Only clan owners may change ownership.
permission-help-group-create = Create groups. The creator joins their new group and may manage it while they remain a clan member.
permission-help-group-rename = Change group names and colors, without changing permissions or membership.
permission-help-group-delete = Delete custom groups and end the access their grants provide. Built-in groups cannot be deleted.
permission-help-group-assign = Add or remove members. They gain or lose the group's permissions, including Secrets shared with it. Adding yourself to someone else's group requires clan ownership.
permission-help-group-inspect-assignments = Allow people in this group to see who belongs to each group.
permission-help-atlas-create = Create clan folders. Access inside each folder must be assigned there; this gives no access to existing maps.
permission-help-package-create = Create clan-owned packages. Editing and publishing require permissions on the new package. Other packages have their own permissions.
permission-help-atlas-read = See this folder. Reading the maps inside still requires Read maps.
permission-help-atlas-rename = Rename this folder. Its maps and their permissions stay in place.
permission-help-atlas-delete = Delete this folder under the clan's folder deletion rules. Only clan owners hold this permission.
permission-help-atlas-accept-filing = Allow maps to be moved into this folder. Moving a map also requires permission to move that map out of its current folder.
permission-help-atlas-accept-transfer = Move maps you own into this clan folder. Choose whether the clan owns them or you keep ownership. Existing map shares end.
permission-help-area-create = Create clan-owned maps in this folder. The creator can edit the new map; clan owners retain ownership authority.
permission-help-area-create-member-owned = Create Member-owned maps here. Their recorded owners control access; folder permissions and clan ownership do not reveal them.
permission-help-area-read = Read ordinary map content. This reveals no Secrets or other people's Private additions. Reading a Secret also requires access to its map. On Member-owned maps, Read stays on while any other map permission is granted.
permission-help-area-add = Add ordinary map content. Reading the map is still required. This gives no permission to edit existing content or write in Secrets.
permission-help-area-edit = Change existing ordinary map content. Reading the map is still required. Secret content has separate editing permissions.
permission-help-area-remove-content = Remove ordinary map content. Removing a map room also removes additions attached to it, including Secret and Private additions. This does not permit deleting the whole map.
permission-help-area-rename = Rename the map without changing its ownership or content.
permission-help-area-refile = Move this map to another clan folder that permits maps to be moved in. The destination's permissions may change who can access it.
permission-help-area-delete = Delete the whole map, including its Secrets and Private additions. This is separate from removing ordinary content.
permission-help-area-copy = Make an independent copy. A Secret comes along only with its own Copy permission; other people's Private additions never do.
permission-help-area-share-external = Give outside friends view-only access to a clan-owned map, without editing, copying or Secrets. The share ends when its sharer leaves or loses this permission.
permission-help-secret-create-member-owned = Create Member-owned Secrets on a readable map. Their owners choose who can access them; clan ownership alone gives no access.
permission-help-secret-create-clan-owned = Create Clan-owned Secrets on readable clan-owned maps. The creator can read, add and edit their new Secret. Clan owners retain full authority.
permission-help-secret-read = Read Clan-owned Secrets on these maps. Reading the underlying map is also required. This never reveals Member-owned Secrets.
permission-help-secret-add = Add content to Clan-owned Secrets. Both the map and the Secret must be readable. Ordinary map content has separate permissions.
permission-help-secret-edit = Change Clan-owned Secret content. Both the map and the Secret must be readable. A map reader can edit a Secret without being able to edit the map itself.
permission-help-secret-remove-content = Remove Clan-owned Secret content. Both the map and the Secret must be readable. This does not permit deleting a whole Secret or changing Member-owned Secrets.
permission-help-secret-manage-access = Inspect and revoke Clan-owned Secret grants, and grant permissions you hold. This gives no ownership or control over Member-owned Secrets.
permission-help-secret-copy = Include Clan-owned Secrets when copying their map. The map also requires Copy permission. Copies become independent of later access changes.
permission-help-grant-inspect = Inspect grants covering this resource and resources within its scope. This does not itself reveal Secret content or allow changing access.
permission-help-grant-manage = Give others access within this scope and the limits below. Only clan owners can grant this permission. It gives no ownership.
permission-help-package-read = List this package in clan resources. Clan members can still install published clan packages by name without this permission. This gives no publishing or editing access.
permission-help-package-edit-draft = Upload and change this package's draft. Publishing requires a separate permission.
permission-help-package-edit-metadata = Change package metadata. Publishing and changing availability require separate permissions.
permission-help-package-manage-availability = Change this package's public availability. Making it public lets people outside the clan discover and download it.
permission-help-package-publish = Publish new versions. Installed users may receive the new code when they update.
permission-help-package-retire = Retire package versions under the registry's rules. This does not delete the whole package.
permission-help-package-delete = Delete the package under the registry's rules. Downloaded copies may remain on other people's devices.
permission-help-read = Read this Secret when its map is also readable. A Secret grant never provides access to the map itself.
permission-help-add = Add content to this Secret. Editing and removing existing content require separate permissions.
permission-help-edit = Change existing Secret content. Ordinary map content has separate permissions.
permission-help-remove = Remove Secret content. This does not permit deleting the whole Secret.
permission-help-manage-access = Inspect and revoke this Secret's grants, and grant permissions you hold. Only owners can appoint access managers or change ownership.
permission-help-copy = Include this Secret in an independent map copy. The map also requires Copy permission. Later revocation cannot remove copies already made.

